<title>FRANCE: Arianespace to launch Japan JSAT satellite.</title>
<headline>Arianespace to launch Japan JSAT satellite.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>European rocket consortium Arianespace said on Friday it had signed a contract to launch the JCSAT-5 satellite for Japan Satellite Systems Inc (JSAT).</p>
<p>The launch is due at the end of 1997 or beginning of 1998 and will be from the Kourou space centre in French Guiana.</p>
<p>The satellite will be the twelfth Japanese launch for Arianespace and its second in the JCSAT series, an Arianespace statement said. The satellite is based on an HS 601 platform from Hughes Space and Communications, a unit of Hughes Electronics Corp. The JSAT contract brings Arianespace's orderbook to 41 launches.</p>
</text>
